Description: Per-clip 3D input corrections in the clip's properties
 "A player adds the input corrections (the input packing, and a per-file 'Swap
 left and right eyes') for every media file shown in 3D, declared or not, since a
 declaration can be wrong", and the correction is kept where the program keeps its
 per-file state: for Kdenlive the project's clip properties. A video clip's
 Properties now offer the stereo layer's "3D Input Format" (every entry of the
 layer's list, in the layer's words and catalogue: Automatic, Not 3D, both eye
 orders of side by side, top and bottom, rows, columns, checkerboard, side by side
 quincunx, frames in turn, both views in one block, the anaglyph pairs and the
 picture-with-depth layouts, those Kdenlive shows as one picture saying so), "Swap
 left and right eyes" for a clip shown in 3D, and "Save the correction into the
 file", which writes the file's own mark (Matroska StereoMode, MP4 st3d) through
 the layer's libstereo-av only when the person presses it, reads it back, then
 takes the correction off the clip and reads the clip again from the file. A clip
 shown flat is offered the list, so an unmarked 3D clip can be declared, but no
 swap and no save. The packing a clip is shown with (monitors, thumbnails, the
 project's conversion, renders) is the file's unless the person corrected it.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-21

